extends RefCounted
## The 49 cuts of the final PV storyboard (Melos_PV_49_Shot_List.csv), each
## tied to the place in 1-10 where it is actually played.
##
##   shot/t        storyboard cut and its second range
##   take          which continuous take it belongs to (tools/promotion/
##                 capture_finale_pv.gd plays a take from its checkpoint)
##   area          course area (level_finale_data.zones())
##   runner        where the runner starts the take (world)
##   setup         initial state of enemies/machines the take relies on
##   camera        world framing: "mode" fixed | follow | track_x | between
##                 "at" world centre (fixed) or offset from the runner,
##                 "zoom" [from, to] (Camera2D zoom; 1.0 shows 1280x720 px
##                 of world), optional "rotation", "shake", "target"
##   move          the camera move the cut asks for
##   phenomenon    what must visibly happen in the cut
##   success       machine-checked condition id (capture tool + probe) and
##                 its meaning
##   overlay       screen regions (fractions of the frame) kept clear of
##                 action for later text/graphics
##
## These rows are the storyboard plan (names, seconds, areas, the cut's
## camera/action text). The PV director (tools/promotion/capture_finale_pv.gd)
## plays each cut from its own play script and camera, and records what it
## actually did -- runner positions, camera samples, events, verdict -- in
## build/promotion/stage-1-10/pv/shots_report.json (copied to
## docs/promotion/stage-1-10/). Slow motion (cuts 4-7) is played in game at
## Engine.time_scale, 60 recorded frames per cut.

static func all() -> Array[Dictionary]:
	var out: Array[Dictionary] = []
	for row in _rows():
		out.append(row)
	return out

